{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef\/takeRef()"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"takeRef","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"VariantRef","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Typically you want to use "},{"code":"g_variant_ref_sink()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"automatically do the correct thing with respect to floating or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-floating references, but there is one specific scenario where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this function is helpful."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The situation where this function is helpful is when creating an API"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"that allows the user to provide a callback function that returns a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":".  We certainly want to allow the user the flexibility to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"return a non-floating reference from this callback (for the case","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"where the value that is being returned already exists).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At the same time, the style of the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" API makes it likely that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for newly-created "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant"},{"type":"text","text":" instances, the user can be saved some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typing if they are allowed to return a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with a floating"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reference."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Using this function on the return value of the user’s callback allows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user to do whichever is more convenient for them.  The caller","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"will always receives exactly one full reference to the value: either","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the one that was returned in the first place, or a floating reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that has been converted to a full reference."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function has an odd interaction when combined with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_ref_sink()"},{"text":" running at the same time in another thread on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Variant"},{"type":"text","text":" instance.  If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_variant_ref_sink()"},{"type":"text","text":" runs first then"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the result will be that the floating reference is converted to a hard"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reference.  If ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_variant_take_ref()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" runs first then the result will"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be that the floating reference is converted to a hard reference and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an additional reference on top of that one is added.  It is best to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"avoid this situation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"takeRef()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"takeRef","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VariantRef","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:4GLib15VariantProtocolPAAE7takeRefAA0bE0VSgyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:4GLib10VariantRefV","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GLib"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef\/VariantProtocol-Implementations"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/variantref\/takeref()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"text":" is floating, sink it.  Otherwise, do nothing.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/VariantRef/takeRef()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/VariantRef\/takeRef()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"takeRef"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib10VariantRefV","text":"VariantRef"},{"text":"!","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/variantref\/takeref()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"takeRef()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"typ